2 CONT The Hedberg Garage was first a whaling station founded by 19th Century produce merchant Olof Hilmer Hedberg, of the site’s namesake. (Obviously.)
2 CONT
2 CONT In jest, Andrew says he’s seen a painting of Olof: “You don’t want to see it – seriously, it is the scariest-looking thing I have ever seen”.
2 CONT
2 CONT “I’ve heard of Norse [Vikings] in their boats and what they used to do – raping and pillaging all over Scotland. This bloke looked like that’s what he came from.”
2 CONT
